# UpVisit Product Context Skill

## Purpose

Use this Skill when designing or redesigning product features for UpVisit.

This Skill gives Figma Make product context for UpVisit so it can make better UX and product decisions without starting from generic event-app, ticketing, CMS, networking, or SaaS assumptions.

This is not a Design System Skill. Use a separate Design System Skill for components, styling, typography, spacing, colours, icons, and visual patterns.

---

## Product Summary

UpVisit is a smart app platform for successful B2B events and offline experiences.

It helps event organisers create and publish digital event experiences with less effort, while giving visitors, exhibitors, sponsors, and speakers a more engaging and measurable experience.

UpVisit combines:

- A self-service CMS platform
- Event apps
- AI-supported content creation
- Interactive 3D maps and navigation
- Event agendas and personalised programmes
- Exhibitor, sponsor, and speaker profiles
- Matchmaking
- Gamification and challenges
- Push notifications
- Participant surveys
- LinkedIn integration
- CRM and ticketing integrations
- Live analytics and engagement data
- White-label and API options

The product is designed to bridge offline and online experiences. It turns physical events, venues, exhibitions, fairs, cultural spaces, city events, and tourism experiences into mobile-first, data-rich, interactive digital experiences.

---

## Core Product Idea

UpVisit helps organisations make offline experiences more successful by adding a digital engagement layer.

The product is not just an event app. It is a platform that connects:

- Event organisers
- Visitors or participants
- Exhibitors
- Sponsors
- Speakers
- Ticketing systems
- CRM systems
- Local places
- Content
- Navigation
- Engagement data
- Commercial opportunities

The main promise is:

More event success with less effort.

UpVisit should feel fast to set up, easy to maintain, and valuable for every stakeholder.

---

## Target Users and Stakeholders

### Event organisers

Event organisers create and manage the digital experience.

Goals:

- Set up an event app quickly
- Reduce manual event work
- Improve visitor experience
- Increase exhibitor and sponsor satisfaction
- Manage complex on-site navigation
- Create digital revenue opportunities
- Track performance in real time

Typical needs:

- Self-service setup
- CMS
- AI-supported content creation
- Agenda management
- Map and navigation setup
- Exhibitor and sponsor management
- Push notifications
- Analytics
- Ticketing and CRM connections

---

### Visitors / participants

Visitors use the app before, during, and after the event.

Goals:

- Find relevant content, sessions, exhibitors, and people
- Navigate the event space
- Build a personal programme
- Discover offers and activities
- Connect with exhibitors or other participants
- Access useful information quickly

Typical needs:

- Interactive map
- 3D navigation
- Search
- Event programme
- Personal agenda
- Push notifications
- Matchmaking
- Exhibitor profiles
- Sponsor content
- Surveys
- Gamification

---

### Exhibitors

Exhibitors use UpVisit to increase visibility and generate leads.

Goals:

- Present their company attractively
- Be discoverable in the app
- Generate leads
- Connect with visitors
- Promote products, offers, or services
- Understand engagement

Typical needs:

- Exhibitor profile
- Multimedia content
- Lead capture
- LinkedIn integration
- Contact options
- Analytics
- Self-service content management

---

### Sponsors

Sponsors use UpVisit to gain digital visibility and measurable value.

Goals:

- Reach event audiences
- Increase brand awareness
- Promote offers or content
- Generate measurable engagement
- Justify sponsorship investment

Typical needs:

- Sponsor profiles
- Digital sponsor packages
- Sponsored placements
- Push notifications
- Content blocks
- Analytics
- Lead generation

---

### Speakers

Speakers are part of the event content experience.

Goals:

- Be visible in the programme
- Share session information
- Connect with attendees
- Support event credibility

Typical needs:

- Speaker profile
- Session links
- Agenda placement
- Contact or social links

---

### Event tech, ticketing, and platform partners

UpVisit can work as an engagement layer for existing ticketing, CRM, or event platforms.

Goals:

- Add visitor engagement beyond ticket transactions
- Avoid building complex app features from scratch
- Offer 3D maps, matchmaking, analytics, and sponsor tools
- Integrate with existing systems
- Expand product suites

Typical needs:

- API integration
- White-label options
- App connection to ticketing or CRM
- Modular features
- Analytics
- Low-friction deployment

---

### Tourism, city marketing, museums, and public spaces

UpVisit can also support cultural, tourism, public-space, and city-based experiences.

Goals:

- Digitise city events, tours, exhibitions, and cultural programmes
- Guide visitors through physical spaces
- Tell location-based stories
- Offer mobile-first local experiences
- Preserve local branding

Typical needs:

- App-based navigation
- Guided routes
- Themed paths
- Location-based content
- Event calendar
- White-label branding
- CMS
- Outdoor and indoor experience support

---

### Agencies and system integrators

Agencies and integrators can use UpVisit as a ready-to-use white-label platform.

Goals:

- Offer event-tech solutions without building from scratch
- Launch quickly for clients
- Use own branding, domain, and user control
- Support public-sector or enterprise innovation projects

Typical needs:

- White-label platform
- API access
- Admin control
- Analytics
- Modular architecture
- Fast setup

